Agy (Google Antigravity) reports quota exhaustion as "Individual quota reached.
Please upgrade your subscription..." rather than the "quota exceeded" phrasing
the classifier expects, so the runtime-fallback hook never fires and agents get
stuck on the dead model.

--- a/packages/model-core/src/runtime-fallback-error-classifier.ts
+++ b/packages/model-core/src/runtime-fallback-error-classifier.ts
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
   /usage\s*quota/i,
   /exhausted\s+your\s+capacity/i,
   /limit\s+exhausted/i,
+  /quota\s+reached/i,
   /all\s+credentials\s+for\s+model/i,
   /cool(?:ing)?\s+down/i,
   /model.{0,20}?not.{0,10}?supported/i,
@@ -115,6 +116,7 @@
     /usage\s+limit/i.test(message) ||
     /credit\s+balance.*too\s+low/i.test(message) ||
     /limit\s+exhausted/i.test(message) ||
+    /quota\s+reached/i.test(message) ||
     /使用上限/.test(message) ||
     /达到.*限制/.test(message) ||
     /额度.*不足/.test(message) ||
